To the maximum extent feasible, the City Council of the City of Baldwin, Georgia provides that its citizens and entities implement the following procedures for handling yard trimmings following the below-described hierarchy:

- (1) Naturalized, low-maintenance landscaping requiring little or no cutting; (2) Grass cycling by mowing it high and letting it lie; (3) Stacking branches into brush piles for use as wildlife habitats and for gradual decomposition into the soil;

- (4) Composting on the site where the material was grown, followed by incorporation of the finished compost into the soil at that site;

- (5) Ifthe procedures outlined within Section 4, subsections (1) to (4) are not utilized by the property owner, tenant or licensee, then the yard trimmings shall be bagged in paper lawn bags or other biodegradable containers and properly disposed of by the property owner, tenant or licensee in a landfill which accepts yard trimmings.
